A||||9||Shaun41178||Ran a 14.8
Z||000000||Shaun41178||05-26-99||11:27 PM||||I went to Milan drgwy in southern michigan today and ran about 6 1/4 miles.  I only won two races but that was not what it was about.  I went up against some tubbed cars so I wasn't planning on winning anyway.  <p>My best time was a 14.8 and best 60' was 2.0<p>I raced a 99 Mustang V6 and beat it without my nitrous.  I did use the nitrous right off the line but after that I didn't.  I ran a 15.9 to his 16.7.  This mustang driver turned a 2.9 60'.  He spun real bad.<p>I also raced an old malibu and got killed as he ran a 13.3<p>I raced a AWD first gen talon and lost to his 14.1<p>I raced a mercury cougar turbo and beat him 14.9 to his 16 flat.  I smoked that guy.<p>I ran a 98 cobra for my last race without nitrous and he ran a 14.2 to my 16.2  I was with him for the first 60 feet though.  It would've been closer with my nitrous but he still would've beat me.<p>This was my first time to a dragstrip so I just tried to enjoy myself.  Which I did very much.  i had a good time.  If anyone lives in NW Ohio or SE mich and would like to meet there for a little racing just let me know.
Z||000001||FieroMike||05-27-99||09:34 AM||||Shaun,<br>Good job! Sounds like you had fun.  Are you running any modifications?  How many miles on the engine?  What type of car? 4spd, 5spd, auto? Later
Z||000002||Eric||05-27-99||05:48 PM||||Hey Shaun, maybe when I get my 3.1 rebuild done I'll take a road trip up to Toledo. Shouldn't be much longer than a two hour drive. Long drives are easy in a Fiero.  I drove my car from Dallas (where I bought it) to Columbus in about 16 hours, stopping every 250 miles for gas!<p>Hey, are you planning on going to the FOCOA national meet in Columbus?  I know the Columbus Fiero club president and he seems to be really excited about it (he's got an 88 GT turbo).  I don't know the web adress for the Columbus Fiero club offhand, but there are links everywhere for it (the club is called COFE Central Ohio Fiero Enthusiests).  They have all the info on the big meet in August.  Maybe I'll see some of you there.
Z||000003||PaUL||05-27-99||06:48 PM||||Wow driving for 16 hours straight, I cant even imagine doing that. You people on the mainland are lucky, you can go anywhere by driving. Here in Hawaii the furthest place is only a 100 mile drive. Also the gas here is $1.60/gal.
Z||000004||theogre||05-27-99||07:01 PM||||Try bracket racing next time.<p>How fast your car goes matters far less in bracket than other classes. In Bracket the only thing that matters is consistancy. You win by making the other guy run outside his bracket times/speeds. You could race a top fuel rail and win if he can't run the bracket.<p>Anyone that tells you it's easy to make a car run every round exactly the same hasn't done it.<p>I hear whining about gas prices again:) Cliff, Tell them what you pay in US$ per gallon. As for $1.60, Mainland prices on the east coast have hit as high as $1.50 lately. many are still over $1.30. So considering the fact that nearly all your gas has to be shipped to you, you're getting off fairly cheep. I have 3 major refiners inside 20 miles, and we're still paying almost that. (Sun[Sunoco], Star[Texaco], and who ever took over the old BP plant)
Z||000005||Shaun41178||05-27-99||11:17 PM||||fieromike:  My engine has roughly 30k on the rebuild.  I bought the engine off of some guy who said it was rebuilt and I believe him cause it runs strong.  I do not know what parts were used in the rebuild cause he had no reciepts.  The only mods are a ignition system and the nitrous.  I hope to get a new cam and rockers in before July 11.  That is when there is a import vs domestic at norwalk.  I hope to run low 14's after those mods are done.  I also have an auto tranny<p>My times are very consistent with my auto and  nitrous use.  I ran a best of 14.8 and a worst of 14.9 so I would be very tough to beat in bracket racing.<p>Eric: If you are up for the drive then i would like to meat you.  I would like to get down for the show in columbus.  I have relatives down there so I could probably work something out with them.  I am leaving my schedule open but don't know what it will look like 2 months from now.  I would also like to meet Jerry Isbell and see his turbo Fiero.  I don't live in Michigan I actually live in Toledo so you might be closer then 2 hours.
Z||000006||LEE498||05-28-99||02:41 PM||||SHAUN, be sure to fill us in about what happens in NORWALK.
